=================================
 22PN data files for Mathematica 
=================================

This directory holds the supplementary data files for Ref.[1], in which 
gravitational waves radiated from a particle of mass mu in circular 
orbits around a Schwarzschild black hole of mass M to the 22nd 
post-Newtonian (PN) order have been derived. It has been checked that 
the data files can be used in Mathematica 8.0. 
To use data files, it is recommended to follow "Usage" below in order to 
suppress large expressions of the PN expansions.

Files
-----

The following data files contain the PN expressions for the total energy 
flux to infinity, the modal energy flux and the waveforms as a function of 
v=(M/r_0)^(1/2) where r_0 is the orbital radius of the particle. 
The expressions also contain the mathematical constant Pi=3.14159..., 
the Euler's constant EulerGamma=0.57721... and the Zeta function Zeta[n], 
where n is the positive integer.

* dEdt_inf_22PN.nb  

  This Mathematica file contains the 22PN expression for the gravitational wave 
energy flux to infinity dEdt8, which is normalized by the quadrupole formula 
(32/5)*(\mu/M)*v^(10). One can compare dEdt8 with the 5.5PN expression 
in Ref.[2]. 

* etalm_22PN.nb  

  This Mathematica file contains the 22PN expressions for the modal energy flux 
eta[l,m], which are normalized by the quadrupole formula, where 2<=l<=24 
and 1<=m<=l. One can compare eta[l,m] with the 5.5PN expressions in Ref.[2]. 

* rholm_22PN.nb

  This Mathematica file contains the 22PN expressions for the factorized waveforms 
proposed in Ref.[3]. One will find the amplitude rho[l,m] and the phase 
delta[l,m] of the waveforms, where 2<=l<=46 and 1<=m<=l, in this file. 
One can compare rho[l,m] and delta[l,m] with the 5.5PN expressions in Ref.[4]. 

Usage
-----

* dEdt_inf_22PN.nb  

  To use the data in the file "dEdt_inf_22PN.nb", type the commands 
in a new Mathematica session as:

  << "dEdt_inf_22PN.nb";
  Series[dEdt8,{v,0,4}]
                  2                    4
            1247 v          3   44711 v        5
        1 - ------- + 4 Pi v  - -------- + O[v]
              336                 9072

* etalm_22PN.nb

  To use the data in the file "etalm_22PN.nb", type the commands 
in a new Mathematica session as:

  << "etalm_22PN.nb";
  Series[eta[2,2],{v,0,4}]
                 2                   4
            107 v          3   4784 v        5
        1 - ------ + 4 Pi v  + ------- + O[v]
              21                1323

* rholm_22PN.nb

  To use the data in the file "rholm_22PN.nb", type the commands 
in a new Mathematica session as:

  << "rholm_22PN.nb";
  Series[rho[2,2],{v,0,4}]
                2          4
            43 v    20555 v        5
        1 - ----- - -------- + O[v]
             42      10584

  Series[delta[2,2],{v,0,4}]
           3
        7 v        5
        ---- + O[v]
         3

References
----------

[1] R. Fujita, Prog. Theor. Phys. 128 (2012), 971.

[2] T. Tanaka, H. Tagoshi and M. Sasaki, Prog. Theor. Phys. 96 (1996), 1087. 

[3] T. Damour, B. R. Iyer and A. Nagar, Phys. Rev. D 79 (2009), 064004.  

[4] R. Fujita and B. R. Iyer, Phys. Rev. D 82 (2010), 044051. 

